<section id="section-22-1-conclusion" class="flex flex-col mt-(--spacing-lg) gap-y-(--spacing-sm) scroll-mt-(--spacing-md)"><h2 class="text-(--custom-color-header) scroll-mt-(--spacing-md) [--inline-code-border:] [--inline-code-px:var(--spacing-xs)] [--inline-code-aside-ps:none] [--inline-code-mx:0.1em] break-words font-bold text-4xl mb-(--spacing-sm)">Conclusion</h2><p>I implemented a tiny programming language similar to <span class="italic me-1">BrainF---</span>, while it cannot program any arbitrary <span class="italic me-1">(Turing)</span> program because that requires at least 2 counters, nonetheless it <span class="italic me-1">can</span> print <code class="[word-break:var(--inline-code-word-break,break-word)] inline-block font-mono bg-[var(--inline-code-bg,var(--bg-base-200))] rounded-md text-[var(--inline-code-text,var(--custom-color-text))] px-(--spacing-xs)">Hello World!</code> just using a single variable!</p></section>
