<section id="section-2-1-%60post%60" class="flex flex-col mt-(--spacing-lg) gap-y-(--spacing-sm) scroll-mt-(--spacing-md)"><h2 class="text-(--custom-color-header) scroll-mt-(--spacing-md) [--inline-code-border:] [--inline-code-px:var(--spacing-xs)] [--inline-code-aside-ps:none] [--inline-code-mx:0.1em] break-words font-bold text-4xl mb-(--spacing-sm)"><code class="[word-break:var(--inline-code-word-break,break-word)] inline-block font-mono bg-[var(--inline-code-bg,var(--bg-base-200))] rounded-md text-[var(--inline-code-text,var(--custom-color-text))] px-(--spacing-xs)">POST</code></h2><p><code class="[word-break:var(--inline-code-word-break,break-word)] inline-block font-mono bg-[var(--inline-code-bg,var(--bg-base-200))] rounded-md text-[var(--inline-code-text,var(--custom-color-text))] px-(--spacing-xs)">POST</code> is a type of an HTTP request that informs the backend service to create a new resource using the data/payload in the request body.</p><p><code class="[word-break:var(--inline-code-word-break,break-word)] inline-block font-mono bg-[var(--inline-code-bg,var(--bg-base-200))] rounded-md text-[var(--inline-code-text,var(--custom-color-text))] px-(--spacing-xs)">POST</code> is non-idempotent meaning if I send the same request (with the <span class="italic me-1">same</span> payload) multiple items, it may have multiple side effects. In our code this means the <span class="italic me-1">same</span> user would be pushed <span class="italic me-1">multiple</span> times into our <code class="[word-break:var(--inline-code-word-break,break-word)] inline-block font-mono bg-[var(--inline-code-bg,var(--bg-base-200))] rounded-md text-[var(--inline-code-text,var(--custom-color-text))] px-(--spacing-xs)">users</code> database array.</p></section>
